ex:Ev_Research_Ch19 a backlog:TestEvidence ; rdfs:label "Checks for Research Ch19"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ;
    backlog:attestsCriterion ex:AC_Chapter ; backlog:evidenceVerified true ; backlog:hasTestId "Research/Ch19" ;
    backlog:hasTestSpec "RDODI Stages 1-3 for chapter 19 (Keeping Time, Scheduling Tasks, and Launching Programs), built by 08-tooling/sen0414_ch19_build_run_v1_0_0.py from 08-tooling/sen0414_ch19_rdodi_data_v1_0_5.py: 64 sources (all HTTP 200; the one phrase flagged absent, CRON_TZ on the crontab(5) page, was added deliberately as evidence of absence), 18 findings, a taxonomy of 6 subjects, 19 mid concepts, 65 leaves and 90 document sections. Re-run by the lineage session: Stage1.A 770 triples, Stage1.B 0 violations, Stage2.A 383, Stage2.C conforms, Stage3.A 738, Stage3.F 64 citations verified, Stage3.B conforms, Stage3.E coverage and substance 91, source check 91 real-sourced; overall PASS. Reported by the building agent, not re-run by the lineage session: 92 execution checks with 0 mismatches and HermiT consistent; 13 third-party programs re-run with 0 differing; the chapter page sha256 equals the book ontology's chapterDigest; 12 corpus programs exit 0; eight diagrams all above 0.84; six stories whose links answered HTTP 200; the replay of 75 statements (54 match as printed in Los Angeles, 21 differ: 7 clock, 1 en dash, 13 platform); 11 interpreters (3.11 to 3.14.6 and 3.15.0b4) with 11 items differing; real cron on the container was run (PATH, working directory, environment, TZ and CRON_TZ behaviour observed). NOT EXECUTED: Windows (calc, notepad, mspaint, start, Task Scheduler, schtasks); macOS (open for an app, launchd, launchctl; the plist was only written and read back); a systemd timer (PID 1 is not systemd; only systemd-analyze calendar was run); anything opened by a desktop session, audible sound, a clipboard program, non-C locale names; Python 3.14.7, 3.14.8 and final 3.15.0; ping to nostarch.com (100 percent loss in the sandbox); the pinned book commit; the cron day-field OR rule comes from the Debian man page and the study's own matcher, not from a real cron run. No story photograph (Wikimedia answered 429)." ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "Gates run over the artefacts as committed in 3cb702b (sen0414: chapter 19 (Keeping Time, Scheduling Tasks, and Launching Programs) research package at the CME standard); the gates re-run by the lineage session at 2026-10-12T23:40:22 UTC." ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "08-tooling/sen0414_rdodi_gates_v1_1_1.py (rdodi-ecosystem/02-gates/rdodi_pipeline_validator_v1_6_0.py, Stages 1-3), sen0414_rdodi_checks_v1_2_0.py (Python 3.14.x; HermiT)" ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-10-12T23:40:47"^^xsd:dateTime .
