ex:Ev_Research_Ch20 a backlog:TestEvidence ; rdfs:label "Checks for Research Ch20"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ;
    backlog:attestsCriterion ex:AC_Chapter ; backlog:evidenceVerified true ; backlog:hasTestId "Research/Ch20" ;
    backlog:hasTestSpec "RDODI Stages 1-3 for chapter 20 (Sending Email, Texts, and Push Notifications), built by 08-tooling/sen0414_ch20_build_run_v1_0_0.py from 08-tooling/sen0414_ch20_rdodi_data_v1_0_1.py: 72 sources (all HTTP 200, checked for the passages relied on), 15 findings, a taxonomy of 6 subjects, 20 mid concepts, 65 leaves and 91 document sections. Re-run by the lineage session: Stage1.A 776 triples, Stage1.B 0 violations, Stage2.A 387, Stage2.C conforms, Stage3.A 746, Stage3.F 72 citations verified, Stage3.B conforms, Stage3.E coverage and substance 92, source check 92 real-sourced; overall PASS. Reported by the building agent, not re-run by the lineage session: 89 execution checks with 0 mismatches and HermiT consistent; 12 corpus programs exit 0, of which seven use a local stand-in (aiosmtpd for SMTP; real ezgmail against a stand-in whose replies the agent wrote; a recorder in place of ntfy); eight diagrams all at 0.84 or more; six stories whose links answered HTTP 200; the replay of the chapter's statements (38 of 46 match in the zone Europe/Istanbul on the stand-in). The building agent states that after its last text edit it did not re-run its comparison of finding F13 (what changed in Python) with the section text, and that the figures of F3 (the Istanbul replay), F15 (the not-done list) and F1 (hash and byte counts) are carried only in the findings, not in the sections. NOT EXECUTED: any real Gmail account, Google Cloud project, consent screen or token refresh (the 7-day expiry of a Testing refresh token is read from Google's page, not run); any connection to Gmail's servers (imap and smtp.gmail.com timed out); whether Gmail accepts .exe or .zip attachments; any text message (no phone number, carrier gateway or Twilio account; Twilio answered 401 without credentials); any publication to ntfy.sh or the ntfy app (only GETs for health and an unused topic); the 153 and 67 character segment sizes for long texts come from arithmetic and no page states them (flagged unconfirmed); Windows and macOS; Python 3.14.7 and later; the pinned book commit. The Gmail replies, the ntfy reply bodies and the HTML samples used by the stand-ins were written by the building agent; only the shapes of the HTTP exchanges were checked, not Google's or ntfy's actual replies. No story photograph (Wikimedia answered 429)." ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "Gates run over the artefacts as committed in 5146f8f (sen0414: chapter 20 (Sending Email, Texts, and Push Notifications) research package at the CME standard); the gates re-run by the lineage session at 2026-10-13T06:56:27 UTC." ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "08-tooling/sen0414_rdodi_gates_v1_1_1.py (rdodi-ecosystem/02-gates/rdodi_pipeline_validator_v1_6_0.py, Stages 1-3), sen0414_rdodi_checks_v1_2_0.py (Python 3.14.x; HermiT)" ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-10-13T06:56:54"^^xsd:dateTime .
