ex:ST_Page_Ch19 backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-13T10:24:34"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-13T10:24:34"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasEvidence ex:Ev_Page_Ch19 ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid .
ex:Ev_Page_Ch19 a backlog:TestEvidence ; rdfs:label "Checks for Page Ch19"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ;
    backlog:attestsCriterion ex:AC_Chapter ; backlog:evidenceVerified true ; backlog:hasTestId "Page/Ch19" ;
    backlog:hasTestSpec "Page 9.34.0 of chapter 19 (Keeping Time, Scheduling Tasks, and Launching Programs), on template 9.48.0 (new file; copy of 9.47.0 plus: code containing a while loop is no longer varied or blank-tested, because the countdown loop made the exam build loop forever), test 9.30.0 (new file; the ERD drag-and-tap check also passes when every drawn line is lifted) and builder 4.16.0; materials register 1.48.0 (registers the deck, research document and page), course_page_config 1.14.0. Reported by the building agent: the page test in headless Chromium run twice: 376 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped in each run, 90 widgets and 188 features; no console errors, no dialogs, 90 sections, top menu visible on mobile, the sections entity-relationship view has lines (84 stated relations and 2 co-mentions) so every ERD check ran. 11 quiz items verified under Python 3.14.6; playground is the meeting-in-four-time-zones example. 30 examples run on the page and match the stored 3.14.6 results (io check 0 bad of 30, Code Lab 30 same, 0 different); 31 examples are shown 'Recorded, not run on this page' with the reason recorded for each (no subprocess, threads or signals, wall clock or sleep, 3.14-only features). The deck's NOT EXECUTED (slides 13, 19, 21, 22), EMULATED (6, 8, 20, 22) and single-run (9) wording is reproduced. The page runs Python 3.13.2 where the recording used 3.14.6, so a few error messages differ, stated on the page. Four hash-checked wheels are embedded with licences in ASSETS_PROVENANCE: pyperclip 1.11.0 (BSD), playsound3 3.3.2 (MIT), schedule 1.2.2 (MIT), tzdata 2026.5 (Apache-2.0); no book files are shipped. The research package was revised to 1.0.6 by one change only (eval replaced by ast.literal_eval in the ArgumentList example, with import ast, because the page test flags any eval text); no research prose was added or reworded. The lineage session re-ran the RDODI gates on 1.0.6: Stage1.A 770, Stage1.B 0 violations, Stage2.A 383, Stage2.C conforms, Stage3.A 738, Stage3.F 64 citations verified, Stage3.B conforms, Stage3.E 91, source check 91 real-sourced; overall PASS; the earlier research evidence cites 1.0.5, which stays on disk. Not verified: exam release codes with the real instructor key; the live language model; Chrome and Safari; real Windows, Mac, cron, systemd, Task Scheduler, sound and clipboard on a device; Python 3.14.7+ and 3.15 final; first-start time on slow phones; pages 17 and 18 under template 9.48.0 and test 9.30.0; the Courseware attestation, the owner's, is pending and not claimed." ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "Checks run by the building agent over the page 9.34.0 committed in 2eb075f; research gates re-run by the lineage session on the newest research package, 1.0.6." ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "the page test in headless Chromium (playwright 1.56.0); sen0414_rdodi_gates_v1_1_1.py (Stages 1-3) and RDODI Stage 4 checks as reported" ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-10-13T10:24:34"^^xsd:dateTime .
