ex:ST_Page_Ch20 backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-13T12:52:09"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-13T12:52:09"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasEvidence ex:Ev_Page_Ch20 ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid .
ex:Ev_Page_Ch20 a backlog:TestEvidence ; rdfs:label "Checks for Page Ch20"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ;
    backlog:attestsCriterion ex:AC_Chapter ; backlog:evidenceVerified true ; backlog:hasTestId "Page/Ch20" ;
    backlog:hasTestSpec "Page 9.34.0 of chapter 20 (Sending Email, Texts, and Push Notifications), on template 9.48.0 (unchanged, so no earlier page is affected) and test 9.31.0 (new file: asks 'can you show me that in code?' when 'example' is a concept label; the passage-search wait is 300 s; the ERD check taps an entity that is an end of a drawn relationship; failure detail added to the agents-rank-by-meaning check, which failed once and passed on rerun, so it is timing-sensitive); materials register 1.49.0 (registers the deck, research document and page), course_page_config 1.15.0, page-data 2.18.0 (per-example run limit raised from 20 s to 90 s). Reported by the building agent: the page test in headless Chromium run twice: 376 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped in each run (a first attempt at the second run was killed by an out-of-memory error and rerun clean); no console errors, no dialogs, 91 sections, top menu visible on mobile; ERD checks ran (85 stated relations, 1 co-mention). 11 quiz items covering CO1-CO5. 57 examples: 21 run in the browser and match the stored 3.14.6 result (io check 0 bad of 21, Code Lab 21 same); 36 are shown 'Recorded, not run on this page' with the reason (20 need ezgmail and Google's client library, 6 aiosmtpd, 5 the local ntfy recorder, 2 imaplib examples that need 3.14, 1 time.tzset, 2 subprocess). Stand-ins are labelled visibly; the labels follow the deck plan (NOT EXECUTED slides 5, 6, 8, 14-18, 20, 23; stand-in slides 6, 7, 8, 12, 13, 18, 19, 20, 22, 23). No wheel is embedded: ezgmail is GPLv3+ and not shipped, and Google's client library is a 16.8 MB wheel over the page limit. Research package revised to 1.0.2 as a factual correction: finding F13 and the starttls sentence now say the two verify flags came in Python 3.13 and the TLS 1.2 minimum is older (3.10 per the documentation; 3.11.17 already shows it); the lineage session re-ran the RDODI gates on 1.0.2: Stage1.A 776, Stage1.B 0 violations, Stage2.A 387, Stage2.C conforms, Stage3.A 746, Stage3.F 72 citations verified, Stage3.B conforms, Stage3.E 92, source check 92 real-sourced; overall PASS. The earlier research evidence cites 1.0.1, which stays on disk. KNOWN DEFECT NOT YET FIXED: the deck's slide 15 and the lecture export say 13 of 18 gateway domains have mail exchangers; the building agent re-queried dns.google for all 18 and exactly 12 have MX records (sms.cricketwireless.net only answers aliases), so the research and story text (12) are right and the deck and Lecture tab are wrong; the page's notice says so. Not verified: any real Gmail, phone, ntfy or Twilio; exam release codes with the real instructor key; the live language model; Chrome and Safari; real Windows or macOS; Python 3.14.7+ and 3.15 final; pages 17 to 19 under test 9.31.0; the Courseware attestation, the owner's, is pending and not claimed." ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "Checks run by the building agent over the page 9.34.0 committed in 59efb92; research gates re-run by the lineage session on the newest research package, 1.0.2, against the RDODI ecosystem pinned at commit 89f68596 (the ecosystem has since been restructured upstream, so the gate tool no longer finds its stage vocabularies at head)." ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "the page test in headless Chromium (playwright 1.56.0); sen0414_rdodi_gates_v1_1_1.py (Stages 1-3) and RDODI Stage 4 checks as reported" ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-10-13T12:52:09"^^xsd:dateTime .
