ex:Ev_Deck_Ch21 a backlog:TestEvidence ; rdfs:label "Checks for Deck Ch21"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ;
    backlog:attestsCriterion ex:AC_Chapter ; backlog:evidenceVerified true ; backlog:hasTestId "Deck/Ch21" ;
    backlog:hasTestSpec "Deck 1.0.0 of chapter 21 (Making Graphs and Manipulating Images), 26 slides with speaker notes on every slide (26 of 26, re-counted by the lineage session), built by 08-tooling/ch21-deck/build_v1_0_0.sh under Python 3.14.6 (Pillow 12.3.0, Matplotlib 3.11.2, NumPy 2.5.4, pyperclipimg 0.2.0; the builder and checks run under the system Python 3.13.16). Reported by the building agent: 27 programs ran (12 corpus programs and 15 cuts), all exit 0, the four zip-fetching programs against the cached zip with every file checked by SHA-256; deck_check 41 console rows, 1 chart and 2 tables re-computed, 0 mismatches; program_check 14 panels and 15 programs re-run, 0 mismatches, and 16 pictures on slides checked against what the programs regenerate (16 byte-identical); diagram_check 8 diagrams, 91 labels verbatim; layout 0 overflow; fit 378 frames, 0 overflowing, 0 overlapping; structure_check 0 repairs; honesty_check 0 refusals (6 slides NOT EXECUTED, 4 Recorded, 1 stand-in slide); links 15 opened, all 200. Sixteen stale fixtures (expression, table, chart, program, code, transcript capture, a one-pixel-changed picture, a swapped picture, a wrong caption, a picture no caption names, diagram, and missing NOT EXECUTED, virtual-display, local-stand-in, Recorded and title labels, and a NOT EXECUTED line on an unlisted slide) were each refused by the check that targets them; a re-encoded picture with the same pixels was accepted as pixel-identical, showing the pixel comparison runs. NOT EXECUTED and marked: Windows and macOS rotate fill (slide 11), a Windows folder path (14), Windows, macOS and a real screen for the clipboard (19, run on a virtual display and labelled so), Matplotlib 3.10.0 on Python 3.14.6 (21), and the plt.show() window on a real screen (22, 23). The building agent rendered the deck through LibreOffice and viewed every slide 1 to 26 (slide 17 re-viewed after its last text change; the others on the previous build); first renders had overflow and overlap defects on slides 11, 13-15, 17-19, 21-23, 25 and 26, which were fixed; two small things remain (the zip URL on slide 25 wraps close to the Reference heading; yes/no labels touch a box edge on slides 9 and 13). The commit message says 13 slides carry pictures; the correct count is 12. Not verified: no PowerPoint; the cat picture's licence was not checked (used for teaching only); browser Python was not tried; the slide 21 table runs four interpreters at check time and the picture check needs the cached zip; pictures are compared byte-for-byte with this machine's library versions." ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "Checks run by the building agent over the deck committed in b4fcca5; slide and notes counts re-read by the lineage session at the finish time." ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "08-tooling/ch21-deck: deck_check, program_check, diagram_check, honesty_check, links_check, structure_check and the shared layout, fit and notes checks under Python 3.14.6" ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-10-13T13:55:11"^^xsd:dateTime .
