ex:ST_Deck_Ch22 backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-13T21:37:52"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-13T21:37:52"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasEvidence ex:Ev_Deck_Ch22 ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid .
ex:Ev_Deck_Ch22 a backlog:TestEvidence ; rdfs:label "Checks for Deck Ch22"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ;
    backlog:attestsCriterion ex:AC_Chapter ; backlog:evidenceVerified true ; backlog:hasTestId "Deck/Ch22" ;
    backlog:hasTestSpec "Deck 1.0.0 of chapter 22 (Recognizing Text in Images), 26 slides with speaker notes on every slide (26 of 26, re-counted by the lineage session), built from 08-tooling/ch22-deck under Python 3.14.6 (pytesseract 0.3.13, Pillow 12.3.0, Tesseract 5.3.4). Reported by the building agent: structure_check 0 repairs; deck_check 13 console rows, 2 charts and 3 tables re-computed, 0 mismatches; program_check 16 panels (16 distinct programs) re-run with exit 0 and 14 pictures checked, all byte-identical; diagram_check 8 diagrams, 90 labels verbatim; layout clean; fit 375 frames, 0 overflowing, 0 overlapping; honesty_check 0 refusals (16 programs shown, 1 stand-in slide, 5 NOT EXECUTED slides, 4 Recorded slides); links 11 of 11 answered 200. Sixteen stale fixtures (expression, table, chart, program, code, a one-pixel-changed picture, a swapped picture, a wrong caption, a picture no caption names, diagram, and missing NOT EXECUTED, stand-in, local-stand-in, Recorded and title labels, and a NOT EXECUTED line on an unlisted slide) were each refused by the check that targets them; a re-encoded picture control was accepted (13 byte-identical, 1 pixel-identical); there is no transcript-only fixture because no panel shows a transcript without its program. NOT EXECUTED and marked on slides 7, 15, 19, 22 and 23; the screen program on slide 22 ran on a labelled virtual display. The building agent rendered the final pptx through LibreOffice and viewed all 26 slides; after one correction (slides 3 and 26 said 17 console rows, only 13 are shown and checked, now 13) it re-ran every check and fixture but did not re-look at slides 3 and 26; slides 23 and 14 are tight but pass. Differences from the research: the deck's accuracy numbers come from 900-pixel pages while the research's 8 px, 12 px, noise and Otsu numbers came from 700-pixel pages, so the deck prints its own; the research's page-segmentation-mode-7 figure (0.9923) was not re-run; the corpus prints 52 pieces for 51 line breaks; the NAPS2 page-slice run reads 'Spam0O', 'Spam1l' and 'Spamo6'; the hyphen program depends on /usr/share/dict/words of this machine. The 12 corpus programs were run but are not shown (lines wider than a slide); two of the six stories are in the notes only. Not verified: no PowerPoint; Windows, macOS, a real screen and a scanner; Python 3.15, source-only pytesseract pins and the language-model step; slide 23 counts and the 'recorded on 13 Oct' statements are recorded results, not run during the build; the full build script timed out in its last stretch (10-minute foreground limit), so the committed pptx comes from the last manual run of the remaining steps and fixtures with the same commands, not from one uninterrupted script run." ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "Checks run by the building agent over the deck committed in 3f4fcb8; slide and notes counts re-read by the lineage session at the finish time." ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "08-tooling/ch22-deck: deck_check, program_check, diagram_check, honesty_check, links_check, structure_check and the shared layout, fit and notes checks under Python 3.14.6" ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-10-13T21:37:52"^^xsd:dateTime .
