ex:Ev_Research_Ch23 a backlog:TestEvidence ; rdfs:label "Checks for Research Ch23"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ;
    backlog:attestsCriterion ex:AC_Chapter ; backlog:evidenceVerified true ; backlog:hasTestId "Research/Ch23" ;
    backlog:hasTestSpec "RDODI Stages 1-3 for chapter 23 (Controlling the Keyboard and Mouse), built by 08-tooling/sen0414_ch23_build_run_v1_0_0.py from 08-tooling/sen0414_ch23_rdodi_data_v1_0_2.py: 56 sources (all HTTP 200), 22 findings, a taxonomy of 6 subjects, 24 mid concepts, 74 leaves and 104 document sections. Re-run by the lineage session: Stage1.A 865 triples, Stage1.B 0 violations, Stage2.A 439, Stage2.C conforms, Stage3.A 850, Stage3.F 56 citations verified, Stage3.B conforms, Stage3.E coverage and substance 105, source check 105 real-sourced; overall PASS. Reported by the building agent, not re-run by the lineage session: 91 execution checks with 0 mismatches and HermiT consistent; the comparison of findings with section text, run after the last text edit, found no finding with a figure missing from the section text; 12 corpus programs exit 0, each on its own virtual X display (Xvfb, with openbox where needed), labelled 'virtual display, not a real screen'; eight diagrams all at 0.85 or more; six stories whose Wikipedia links answered HTTP 200; the third-party record replays 80 statements; 12 interpreters and 27 items compared (MouseInfo breaks on Tk 9; scroll units differ between Tk 9.0.3 and 8.6.14; PyScreeze returns None up to 0.1.29 and raises from 0.1.30; PyAutoGUI 0.9.40, and 0.9.41 with PyScreeze 1.0.1, fail at import). NOT EXECUTED: a real screen, Windows permissions and SendInput, macOS permissions and Quartz, HiDPI, multi-monitor hardware, applications that block synthetic input and a real Wayland compositor (X11, SendInput and Quartz behaviour rests on primary documents only); the logout hotkeys, the Sushi Go Round game and CAPTCHA solving; no Tk window opens on the uv builds of 3.14.0 and 3.14.1 and 3.11.17 has no tkinter, so Tk behaviour was observed on 3.14.6 and Ubuntu 3.12 only; the message-box program answers a confirm dialog through xdotool and does not drive prompt or password; of 13 external links in the live record 7 answered 200, 3 